From df1ba0860f04a8eaad152be85d34c85b453e50ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:22:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): require every expected CI check before review,
 carry or merge; tri-state launcher CI read

Sentinel issue #154. GitHub creates a `needs:` job's check run only once its
dependencies finish (ai.ubq.fi `verify-artifact` needs `validate`,
`mac-containment` and `darwin-native`), so a head whose existing runs were
all green read green before its required job existed: live, the carried head
f0008beb62 of PR 1064 showed three of three runs green from 08:41:53Z to
08:41:58Z. A CI-first poll in that window requested a review, a carried poll
wrote the carried-merge marker, and a launcher read merged.

One pure rule (`missingExpectedChecks`, src/repair/ci-coverage.ts): a head
must report every check name of each check suite of the base it is tested
against that shares a check name with it. Unshared base suites (sentinel
`development` holds a `dispatch` run per five-minute schedule) and commit
statuses are never expected.

Runtime (generation 81):
- The base is read through a new lenient port read, `readCheckSuites` (name
  and `check_suite.id` of each check run; exact head and item bound kept, no
  label bound, no commit statuses), never through the strict CI read, whose
  64-character label bound refuses every live sentinel `development` tip
  (78-character `matrix_cell (<cellId>)` runs of supervisor.yml: 7 of 22 on
  9a1b1d924, 33 of 75 on 3f041b46d). The strict `readChecks` stays R80's.
- The sentinel self scope reads no base, like the launcher: its gate is the
  one named `test-local` job.
- CI-first review gate: a green head is reviewed only once it covers the
  record's base; otherwise the existing bounded `ci_pending` wait and park
  (`CI did not finish before review within 6 hours: verify-artifact(absent)`),
  uncharged.
- Ceiling moved-base read: the spent reviewed head is refreshed only once it
  covers its reviewed base (waits at `delivery`, REVIEWED_CI_PENDING park).
- Carried step: the carried-merge marker is written only once H1 covers T
  (CARRIED_CI_PENDING park).
- A base listing that cannot be read waits and parks the same way at all
  three steps (`base checks unreadable`), never a deferral without a write.

Launcher (ops/, may ship before the runtime; imports only the pure rule):
- `hasAllChecksGreen(head, base?)` is tri-state: true green, false read and
  not green, null unreadable (incomplete, failing, malformed or empty
  listing of the head or the base).
- `preMergeGate` passes the reviewed base and `carriedMergeGate` passes T, so
  a marker written in the gap by R80 merges nothing (`checks_pending`).
- The retry pass reads foreign CI-parked heads against their record base,
  adds a head to `ciReadHeads` only after a successful non-empty listing, and
  plans no CI correction or CI fix for an unreadable one (`ciUnreadHeads`).

Tests drive the CI-first gate, the ceiling's moved-base read and the carried
step through the real GitHub port over the live 9a1b1d924 and 3f041b46d
listings (tests/fixtures/repair), for the self scope and a foreign one.

Rollback: every write is an R80 shape (`ci_pending` waits, parks under the
existing prefixes); the tests parse every write under R80 e48e7e110 and run
R80's own `preReviewCiParked` over the new parks, guarded on the R80 source
being present (gen80 helpers added beside the gen79 ones).

